      "claim": "Ketanserin, the closest structural analog sharing the 4-fluorophenyl ketone, piperidine, and cyclic-urea motif, has absolute oral bioavailability 49.3 ± 18.0% (range 27–69%) by AUC and about 60% by F = 1 − E in fasted subjects, both above the 20% threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C17","C19"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Sertindole, combining piperidine, fluorophenyl, and cyclic-urea heterocycle, has oral bioavailability approximately 74–75%; L2 records show tablet relative bioavailability about 75% and tablet-to-solution near unity.",
      "card_ids": ["C07","C08","C11","C20","C22","C31"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Trazodone, sharing a propyl-linked azole-fused cyclic amide and aryl piperazine/piperidine-like scaffold, has absolute oral bioavailability 63–91% across fasted and fed groups; crossover records report 63–65%.",
      "card_ids": ["C02","C05","C10","C15","C03","C24","C25","C30","C32"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Maraviroc, a piperidine-containing oral drug, has population F estimates of 0.24 at 100 mg fasted and 33% at 600 mg, both above threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C16","C21","C29"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Additional L1/L2 records for setipiprant (≥50% human; 32–55% rat; 55% dog), PBA (78%), cerivastatin (60%), BAL27862 (>80%), and encainide (76–78% in cirrhosis) all exceed the threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C14","C23","C26","C01","C28","C06","C13","C04","C09","C12","C18","C27","C33"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4/L5 absorption evidence: DMP, which shares the benzimidazolone-piperidine-propyl fragment with the query, has Caco-2 Papp A→B >1×10^-5 cm/s, solubility 5.898 mg/mL in Tween 20, and 100% release from SEDDS; L5 also shows high permeability and efflux ratios near 1.0 for several non-query compounds.",
      "card_ids": ["C49","C51","C52","C65","C59","C61","C62","C63","C67","C60","C68","C64","C66","C58"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No affirmative threshold-relevant evidence supports F < 20% for the query; the physicochemical prior flags ionization/low logD as an absorption liability, but this is not endpoint proof and is outweighed by transferable direct L1 outcomes.",
      "card_ids": ["C17","C19","C07","C08","C02","C05","C10","C15","C16","C21","C29","C14","C01","C06","C04"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "gut_wall_efflux_intestinal_metabolism",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C58","C59","C60","C61","C62","C63","C64","C65","C66","C67","C68","C69"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement exists for the exact query molecule (benperidol-like butyrophenone/piperidine benzimidazolone).",
    "No query-specific gut-wall efflux or intestinal metabolism data; L5 records are for other molecules and mostly report permeability rather than metabolism.",
    "Formulation and prandial state for the query are unspecified, while several supporting records are formulation- or prandial-state-dependent.",
    "First-pass metabolism and clearance for the query are not measured; the physicochemical prior flags an absorption liability due to complete ionization and low logD, but this is not affirmative evidence for F < 20%.",
    "Structural transfer from analogs is qualitative; no exact structural match is present in the record set."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) because multiple transferable L1 absolute-oral-bioavailability records for close structural analogs—ketanserin (49–60%), sertindole (~74–75%), trazodone (63–91%), maraviroc (24–33%), setipiprant (≥50% human), PBA (78%), cerivastatin (60%), BAL27862 (>80%), and encainide (76–78%)—meet or exceed the threshold, and no affirmative evidence supports F < 20%. L5 adds only indirect, mostly non-query-specific high-permeability/no-efflux records; they do not overturn the prior. Confidence remains moderate."
}

